    "text": "To determine the number of students Beth had in her class at the end of her final year, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Start with the initial number of students in Beth's class.\n2. Add the number of students who joined the following year.\n3. Subtract the number of students who left in the final year.\n\nLet's go through the calculations step by step:\n\n1. The initial number of students is 150.\n2. The number of students who joined the following year is 30. So, we add 30 to 150:\n   \\[\n   150 + 30 = 180\n   \\]\n3. The number of students who left in the final year is 15. So, we subtract 15 from 180:\n   \\[\n   180 - 15 = 165\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of students Beth had in her class at the end of her final year is \\boxed{165}.",
